/* Voice capture (docs/requirements/fase-2/17-captura-voz.md). English; the
   development language. The speech string names Apple on purpose: when the
   device cannot transcribe on its own, iOS sends the audio to Apple, and a
   string that hid that would be false. Neither the audio nor the transcript
   is ever stored. */
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "So you can dictate an expense instead of typing it. The audio is never stored.";
"NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription" = "To turn what you dictate into text and fill in the expense form. If your iPhone cannot do it on its own, iOS sends that audio to Apple to transcribe it.";
